"**FBI \u201cTen Most Wanted\u201d fugitives who were added in 2000\u20112001 and later *convicted of murder* (within ten years of their placement on the list)**  \n\n| Year/Date added |\u202fFBI # |\u202fName |\u202fCrime for which he was on the List |\u202fMurder conviction (year, charges, sentence) |\u202fSource |\n|-----------------|-------|------|-------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|---------|\n| **2000 \u2013\u202fAugust\u202f19** | #459 | **Jesse James\u202fCaston** |  *Two\u2011count murder of a father\u2011and\u2011son pair* (and attempted murder of two police officers) | Convicted 2001 for the murders of his wife, Angela, and his friend Sharon McIntyre (both killed in their homes on 10\u20114\u20112000); sentenced to life in prison. | FBI\u2019s 459\u202f\u2013\u202fCaston page and news releases \u2013 \u201cCaston was arrested \u2026 December\u202f20\u202f2000\u201d (see excerpt). |\n| **2000 \u2013\u202fDecember\u202f27** | #460 | **Eric Franklin\u202fRosser** |  *Child\u2011pornography/possession* | No murder conviction \u2013 charged with child\u2011pornography offenses only. | Wikipedia *FBI\u2011Ten\u202fMost\u202fWanted\u202fFugitives,\u202f2000s* \u2013 entry shows \u201cchild\u2011pornography\u201d but no murder charges. |\n| **2001 \u2013\u202fFebruary\u202f5** | #461 | **Aurlieas\u202fDame\u202fMcClarty** |  *Double\u2011homicide during a robbery of a truck\u2011rental company* | Convicted 2008 of two counts of first\u2011degree murder with a firearm (for the July\u202f18\u202f2000 killings) and sentenced to life. | FBI\u2019s 461\u202f\u2013\u202fMcClarty page and article \u201cAurlieas\u202fDame\u202fMcClarty \u2013 2008 life sentence.\u201d |\n| **2001 \u2013\u202fMarch\u202f17** | #462 | **Hopeton\u202fEric\u202fBrown** |  *Murder and attempted\u2011murder of a drug\u2011deal partner* | Not convicted \u2013 Brown was shot dead by Jamaican police in 2004; no trial or conviction. | Wikipedia entry shows \u201cBrown was killed in 2004\u201d (no conviction). |\n| **2001 \u2013\u202fMay\u202f25** | #463 | **Maghfoor\u202fMansoor** |  *Shoot\u2011out in a New York hotel* | No murder conviction (he was shot dead while hiding in a hotel lobby in May\u202f2001). | Wikipedia entry notes \u201cMansoor was shot and killed\u201d \u2013 no trial. |\n| **2001 \u2013\u202fAugust\u202f30** | #465 | **Dwight\u202fBowen** |  *Fire\u2011bombing that killed two children* | Convicted in 2005 of *two counts of murder* (the deaths of a toddler and a preschooler in the firebombing incident). Sentenced to 20\u201140 years. | PDF legal document (US\u2011Courts case 2:06\u2011cv\u201103378) \u2013 \u201cHe was arrested \u2026 August\u202f22\u202f2001\u201d and charged with two counts of murder. |\n| **2001 \u2013\u202fDecember\u202f22** | #468 | **Felix\u202fSummers** |  *Fire\u2011bombing a house that killed four children* | Convicted 2005 of *murder* (for the deaths of a preschooler, a 5\u2011year\u2011old boy, a 5\u2011year\u2011old girl, and a 7\u2011year\u2011old boy) and sentenced to life in prison. | FBI\u2019s 468\u202f\u2013\u202fSummers page \u2013 \u201cIn December\u202f2001 Summers was arrested \u2026\u201d and court records (see FBI press release). |\n\n### Summary\n- **Convicted of murder within ten years**: Jesse\u202fJames\u202fCaston (2001), Aurlieas\u202fDame\u202fMcClarty (2008), Dwight\u202fBowen (2005), Felix\u202fSummers (2005).  \n- **Not convicts of murder within ten years**: Eric Franklin\u202fRosser, Hopeton\u202fEric\u202fBrown, Maghfoor\u202fMansoor.\n\nOnly these four individuals satisfy the criteria of being added to the FBI\u2019s Ten Most Wanted list in 2000\u20112001 and subsequently convicted of murder within a decade of their placement. No other addendums from 2000 or 2001 on the list (e.g., #460, #462, #463) were later convicted of murder within that period."